"""Micras encoder board edge tab: the encoder board's side of the board-to-board joint.

The encoder board stands upright in a slot in the main board. Its 5.0 x 1.0 mm
tab carries 4 pads per side (2.0 x 0.6 mm, 0.95 mm pitch) that are soldered to
the main board pads beside the slot. Pads 1-4 are on the bottom side and pads
5-8 on the top (chip) side. Pinout and pads: the Altium EncoderLib
ENCODER_CONN (MicrasEncoder.PcbDoc J1), so a board built from this package fits
the main board's EncoderSlot.

Footprint frame: origin at the pad centres, which sit 0.2 mm above the
shoulder line (the main board's top surface), so the pads run from 0.8 mm into
the slot to 1.2 mm above it and end 0.2 mm from the tab edge. The footprint's
-X points into the slot: placed at 90 degrees, the tab edge is at the bottom
and, seen from the chip side, pads 1/5 are on the right.

The tab is copper on the PCB itself, not a purchased part: it is excluded from
the BOM and the placement file.
"""

load("@stdlib/interfaces.zen", "Spi")

VDD = io(Power)
GND = io(Ground)
SPI = io(Spi)
A = io(Net)
B = io(Net)

Component(
    name="TAB",
    prefix="J",
    symbol=Symbol(library="EncoderTab.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("ENCODER_CONN.kicad_mod"),
    pins={
        "CSn": SPI.CS,
        "CLK": SPI.CLK,
        "MISO": SPI.MISO,
        "MOSI": SPI.MOSI,
        "VDD": VDD,
        "GND": GND,
        "A": A,
        "B": B,
    },
    skip_bom=True,
)
